      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## wan-s2v.json\n\nAn audio-driven performance: our character performs an audio file\n\n**Does:** a still **portrait** + an audio file -> a clip of the character *performing* it - head movement, expression and articulation (`WanSoundImageToVideo`, Wan2.2-S2V-14B). Broader than S32's lip-sync: the whole performance is audio-driven. The output **carries the audio** (aac). Host: `Wan2_2-S2V-14B_fp8_e4m3fn_scaled_KJ` (16.65 GB, Apache-2.0) + **`wav2vec2_large_english`** audio encoder (631 MB - a different encoder from S32's chinese-base) + the **Wan2.2 4-step lightning lora** (1.23 GB - not our lightx2v I2V lora) + umt5/VAE.\n**Measured (E16, 2026-10-11):** a 5-s clip (80 frames at 16 fps) in **140 s** - the 4-step lora recipe. Identity holds through the performance (head tilts, blinks, mouth). Canvas **640x640** - a square portrait fits exactly.\n**Knobs:** the **audio** (drives the performance - trim it to `seconds`, see Traps); the **reference** (portrait, face clear); **`seconds`** on `PrimitiveFloat` (5.0 ships) - a `ComfyMathExpression` turns it into **`length`** rounded to the model's required 4n+1 (`max(73,floor((a*16-4)/4+0.5)*4+1)`; the -4 compensates the first-frame hack's +3 output frames, and 73 is the model's floor, so the shortest clip this flow makes is 4.75 s). Sampling: **4 steps / cfg 1.0 / uni_pc / simple** with the Wan2.2 4-step lora. **fps is pinned at 16** on `CreateVideo` - the audio bucket is built for 16-fps video in the node code, so any other fps would desync the performance; it is deliberately not a knob.\n**Traps:** the checkpoint keeps its **as-downloaded name** (`Wan2_2-S2V-14B_fp8_e4m3fn_scaled_KJ.safetensors` - the template's Kijai-original name is a different string). The audio encoder is per-route: S32 uses chinese-base, this flow uses large-english. Only the FIRST `length` frames' worth of audio conditions the motion (out-of-range frames read as silence) while `CreateVideo` muxes the whole audio file - **trim your audio to `seconds`** or the tail plays over motionless frames. The `LatentCut`/`LatentConcat` pair is the template's **first-frame duplication hack** (double latent frame 0, drop the first decode - that is where the +3 output frames come from), not extend plumbing: longer audio chains through **`WanSoundImageToVideoExtend`**, which this flow does not wire yet, so one run covers one `seconds`-long chunk.\n**Siblings:** `wan-infinitetalk.json` (S32) is the lip-sync route; this one performs.\n\n---\n*How to run it: story **S33** in `HOWTO.md`  ·  Why it is this way: **E16** in `video/EXPERIMENTS.md`.*"
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
